### the web interface's runtime, which belongs to the buildsystem and not here
# A development environment serves the pages out of this tree rather than out
# of an install prefix, so what they import has to sit beside them to be
# reachable at all: the modules the interface runs on under the first name, and
# the bundle the docs page loads under the second. On a box both arrive as
# packages.
data/ni-web/vendor/
data/ni-web/swagger/vendor/
### what a file manager leaves behind
# Four of these were committed once and two of them are under data/ni-web,
# where everything is installed onto the box and weighed by a ceiling: they
# were shipped, gzipped, and counted as files of the page.
.DS_Store
### IDE-specific settings
# Visual Studio Code settings
.vscode/
### python environment fallout
venv
### what the Finder leaves behind
# One of these under data/ni-web/app is a file the install rules would ship and
# a case counts, so it is not only clutter.
